-- title:
--   An observer preserving each continuation preserves an early-stopping fold
-- statement:
--   Let $\alpha$ be an input type, $\beta$ a state type, and $\gamma$ an observer-state type. Suppose a charged step $f(b,a)$ returns either a new $\beta$-state or stop, and a charged observed step $g((b,c),a)$ returns either a new pair in $\beta\times\gamma$ or stop. Assume that for all $b\in\beta,c\in\gamma,a\in\alpha$, forgetting the observer in the optional result of $g$ gives exactly the optional result of $f$. Then for every finite input list $l$, $$\operatorname{value}(\operatorname{foldWhile}(g,l,(b,c)))_1=\operatorname{value}(\operatorname{foldWhile}(f,l,b)).$$ A stop signal retains the accumulator entering that step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartDrawProbe.lean#L35-L58

